@startuml "Proxy - Licence (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Proxy — homework 4: three kinds of proxy in one class
interface Application <<Subject>> {
  + launch()
  + open(document)
  + close()
}

class LicenceProxy <<Proxy>> {
  - user : String
  - real : Application
  + launch()
  + close()
  + hasLicence() : boolean
}

class VlsiDesigner <<RealSubject>> {
  + launch()
  + open(document)
}

class LicenceServer {
  - seats : int
  - holders : Set<String>
  - waiting : Deque<String>
  + acquire(user) : boolean
  + release(user) : String
}

class Student

Application <|.. LicenceProxy
Application <|.. VlsiDesigner

note bottom of LicenceProxy
  <b>Three kinds at once.</b>
  <b>Protection</b> — refuses when the seats are gone.
  <b>Virtual</b> — a refused student costs no object.
  <b>Smart reference</b> — close() gives the seat back
  and promotes whoever waited longest.
end note

note bottom of VlsiDesigner
  Holds <b>no reference</b> to LicenceServer.
  The university can buy more seats
  without recompiling it.
end note

note top of Student
  Names <b>Application</b>, and nothing
  on that interface mentions a licence.
end note

Student -[norank]-> Application
LicenceProxy -[norank]-> "0..1" VlsiDesigner : "built only once a seat is granted"
LicenceProxy -[norank]-> LicenceServer : "asks"
Application -[hidden]- LicenceProxy
Application -[hidden]- VlsiDesigner
@enduml
